--- !u!1001 &4155009099287794959
PrefabInstance:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  serializedVersion: 2
  m_Modification:
    serializedVersion: 3
    m_TransformParent: {fileID: 897448338527765495}
    m_Modifications:
    - target: {fileID: 2228702324039901831, guid: c37172f986dc5844584b294312417a62,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "Modern UIs includes a flexible whitelist and permission system that
        allows permissions to be granted manually or automatically and used across
        a wide variety of systems.\n\n<b>Whitelist Types</b>\n\nAt the core of the
        whitelist and permission system are two base scripts that most other whitelist
        components build upon:\n\n<b>1. Whitelist Getter Base</b>\n\u2022 Stores
        player names and whitelist data\n\u2022 Provides multiple ways to access
        whitelist entries\n\u2022 Implements a callback system that notifies other
        scripts whenever the whitelist changes\n\n<b>2. Whitelist Setter Base</b>\n\u2022
        Extends the Whitelist Getter Base\n\u2022 Adds support for modifying whitelist
        data through various methods\n\nThese base scripts are not intended to be
        used directly. Instead, they are implemented by higher-level whitelist types:\n\n<b>1.
        Whitelist</b>\n\u2022 A basic whitelist implementation\n\u2022 Allows for
        having a default / start list of player names\n\u2022 Supports reading and
        modifying whitelist data\n\n<b>2. Synced Whitelist</b>\n\u2022 Synchronizes
        whitelist data across all players\n\u2022 Supports admin whitelists to control
        who is allowed to make changes\n\u2022 Ideal for permissions that you want
        to adjust / change it world and need to stay consistent for everyone in an
        instance\n\nAdditional whitelist sources, editors, combiners, and logic combiners
        are also included and will be covered in later sections."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 2605499191578544654, guid: c37172f986dc5844584b294312417a62,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_AnchorMax.x
      value: 0
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
